      "tasks": [
        "Compare f(-2.1) with f(-3.6).",
        "Compare f(1.3) with f(2.8).",
        "Compare f(x1) and f(x2) for two negative inputs with x2>x1.",
        "Compare f(x1) and f(x2) for two positive inputs with x2>x1.",
        "Identify the negative decreasing and positive increasing input sets."
      ],
      "solution": "On the negative branch, a larger input has a smaller output. Since -3.6<-2.1, f(-2.1)<f(-3.6). On the positive branch, a larger input has a larger output, so f(1.3)<f(2.8). For x1<x2<0, f(x1)>f(x2). For 0<x1<x2, f(x1)<f(x2). The decreasing input set is ]-infinity,0[ and the increasing input set is ]0,+infinity[, using the lesson's transition-point reporting convention.",
