    {
      "source_number": "748",
      "tasks": [
        "Construct the graph of y=17x-2 and classify its monotonicity.",
        "Construct the graph of y=-2.8x+1 and classify its monotonicity."
      ],
      "solution": "For y=17x-2, use distinct points (0,-2) and (1,15) and extend their line in both directions. Its x-intercept is2/17. For x2>x1, the output difference is17(x2-x1)>0, so it increases on the real domain. For y=-2.8x+1, use (0,1) and (1,-1.8); extend their line in both directions. Equivalently -2.8=-14/5, so its x-intercept is5/14. The output difference is(-14/5)(x2-x1)<0, so it decreases on the real domain. Intercepts affect location but not the monotonicity sign.",
