        "Classify all six given functions under the lesson's strict definitions, including the zero-slope boundary case."
      ],
      "solution": "For y=kx+l and x2>x1, f(x2)-f(x1)=k(x2-x1), so the sign of k decides the strict trend. Increasing: y=8x-5 and y=0.01x. Decreasing: y=-3x+10, y=-49x+1000, and y=-(1/12)x. The function y=0x+5 is constantly5: its output difference is0, hence it is neither strictly increasing nor strictly decreasing. The size or sign of l does not change these classifications.",
