      "tasks": [
        "Construct any function on exactly[-5,7] decreasing on[-5,-2[, increasing on]-2,4[, and decreasing on]4,7]."
      ],
      "solution": "One valid construction is the connected broken line through (-5,3),(-2,0),(4,6),(7,3), restricted to -5<=x<=7 with both outer endpoints included and no extension. Equivalently f(x)=-x-2 for-5<=x<=-2; f(x)=x+2 for-2<x<=4; f(x)=10-x for4<x<=7. At-2 the adjacent values agree at0 and at4 they agree at6, so this construction is a well-defined continuous function. The slopes are-1,+1,-1; for two ordered inputs in each required interval their output difference has the corresponding negative, positive, negative sign. Thus every required interval condition holds. This is an example, not a unique answer: the written conditions require neither continuity nor these heights. They exclude-2 and4 from the trend intervals, while the domain still requires one defined function value at each of those two inputs. One cannot infer their heights or mandatory local extrema for every possible source solution solely from the interval conditions.",
